<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>AI-B Trading Desk</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500;600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&family=Anton&family=Oswald:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
</head>
<body>
<div class="app">
  <div class="sidebar">
    <div class="brand">
      <div class="brand-title">AI-B TRADING DESK</div>
      <div class="brand-sub">PERSONAL &middot; PHASE 3</div>
    </div>
    <div class="nav" id="navDesktop"></div>
    <div class="sidebar-foot">
      <p>Decision support only. No live broker feed or auto-execution. No outcome is guaranteed — this tool sharpens judgment, it doesn't replace it.</p>
      <button class="small ghost" id="changeTokenBtn" style="margin-top:10px;width:100%;">Change access token</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="main">

    <div class="page active" id="page-dashboard">
      <div class="page-head"><h1 class="page-title">Dashboard</h1><p class="page-desc">Your desk at a glance. Settings here are the single source of truth — Calculator, Analyze sizing, and the daily risk budget all read from this one place.</p></div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">API Keys<span style="font-size:10px;color:var(--text-dim);font-weight:400;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;">saved on your server, never sent back to this page in full</span></div>
        <div class="field-row3">
          <div class="field">
            <label>Anthropic (Claude) API key <span id="anthKeyStatus" style="color:var(--text-dim);"></span></label>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:6px;">
              <input type="password" id="anthKeyInput" placeholder="sk-ant-...">
              <button class="small" id="anthKeySaveBtn">Save</button>
              <button class="small ghost danger" id="anthKeyClearBtn">Clear</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label>OpenAI API key <span id="openaiKeyStatus" style="color:var(--text-dim);"></span></label>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:6px;">
              <input type="password" id="openaiKeyInput" placeholder="sk-...">
              <button class="small" id="openaiKeySaveBtn">Save</button>
              <button class="small ghost danger" id="openaiKeyClearBtn">Clear</button>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="field">
            <label>OpenRouter API key <span id="openrouterKeyStatus" style="color:var(--text-dim);"></span></label>
            <div style="display:flex;gap:6px;">
              <input type="password" id="openrouterKeyInput" placeholder="sk-or-...">
              <button class="small" id="openrouterKeySaveBtn">Save</button>
              <button class="small ghost danger" id="openrouterKeyClearBtn">Clear</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="disclaimer">Keys entered here are saved server-side (in <code>data/keys.json</code>, alongside your journal — same trust model, same server) and take effect immediately, no restart. They override whatever's in <code>.env</code>. Clearing a key here falls back to <code>.env</code> if one's set there. OpenRouter is one key that gives access to many more model families (Google, Meta, Mistral, DeepSeek, etc.) beyond just Anthropic/OpenAI — optional, not required.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">Account Settings</div>
        <div class="field-row3">
          <div class="field"><label>Account balance ($)</label><input type="number" id="setBalance"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Default risk per trade (%)</label><input type="number" id="setRiskPct" step="0.1"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Daily loss limit (%, prop-firm style)</label><input type="number" id="setDailyLoss" step="0.5"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="field-row">
          <div class="field"><label>Primary AI provider</label>
            <select id="setAiProvider"><option value="anthropic">Anthropic — Claude</option><option value="openai">OpenAI — GPT-4o</option><option value="openrouter">OpenRouter — configurable model</option></select>
          </div>
          <div class="field" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;">
            <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-bottom:9px;">
              <input type="checkbox" id="setFailoverEnabled" style="width:auto;">
              <label style="margin:0;font-size:12px;" for="setFailoverEnabled">Auto-failover to another configured provider if the primary fails</label>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="field" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;max-width:520px;">
          <input type="checkbox" id="setConsensusMode" style="width:auto;">
          <label style="margin:0;" for="setConsensusMode">Consensus mode — run Anthropic + OpenAI together on every Analyze and flag disagreement (needs both keys, ~2x cost/time, overrides failover)</label>
        </div>
        <div id="providerStatusBox" style="font-size:11px;color:var(--text-dim);"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">Recent AI Calls<button class="small ghost" id="refreshLogsBtn">Refresh</button></div>
        <div id="callLogBox"><div class="empty-state">No calls logged yet this session.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3" id="dash-stats" style="margin-top:14px;"></div>

      <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px;">
        <div class="card-title">Live Market View<span style="font-size:10px;color:var(--text-dim);font-weight:400;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;">via TradingView — visualization only, no AI reasoning happens here</span></div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;margin-bottom:6px;">
          <input type="text" id="tvSymbolInput" value="FX:EURUSD" style="flex:1;" placeholder="Paste a TradingView link, or just a symbol like OANDA:XAUUSD">
          <button class="small" id="tvReloadBtn">Load</button>
        </div>
        <div id="tvParseNote" style="font-size:10.5px;color:var(--text-dim);margin-bottom:10px;min-height:13px;"></div>
        <div id="tradingview_chart" style="height:420px;border-radius:var(--radius-sm);overflow:hidden;"></div>

        <details style="margin-top:14px;">
          <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--text-dim);">Show my own drawings/indicators instead — embed a chart you've published on TradingView</summary>
          <div class="disclaimer" style="margin-top:10px;margin-bottom:10px;">TradingView doesn't allow embedding your private saved layout directly (would need your TradingView login inside this page — not something this app will ever ask for). What does work: on tradingview.com, open your chart, use <strong>Publish</strong> → <strong>Copy embed code</strong>, then paste the result below. That's TradingView's own sanctioned way to share a specific chart externally.</div>
          <textarea id="tvEmbedInput" placeholder="Paste the embed code or link TradingView gives you after Publish → Copy embed code" style="min-height:70px;"></textarea>
          <button class="small" id="tvEmbedLoadBtn" style="margin-top:8px;">Embed It</button>
          <div id="tvEmbedNote" style="font-size:10.5px;color:var(--text-dim);margin-top:8px;min-height:13px;"></div>
          <div id="tradingview_published_embed" style="height:420px;border-radius:var(--radius-sm);overflow:hidden;margin-top:8px;"></div>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px;"><div class="card-title">Today's Risk Budget</div><div id="dailyRiskBox"></div></div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px;"><div class="card-title">Recent Journal Entries</div><div id="dash-recent"></div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="page" id="page-analyze">
      <div class="page-head"><h1 class="page-title">Analyze Chart</h1><p class="page-desc">Upload up to 5 timeframes — 5M entry (required), 15M, 1H, 4H, Daily. Higher timeframes set the bias, lower timeframes refine entry timing. Every completed analysis is auto-archived to your historical pattern data. If your Pattern Library has similar past setups for this symbol, they're pulled in as qualitative reference.</p></div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">1 &middot; Upload (5M required, others optional)</div>
        <div class="grid grid-3" id="analyzeUploadSlots"></div>
        <div class="field-row" style="margin-top:16px;">
          <div class="field"><label>Symbol (your best guess — editable)</label><input type="text" id="symbolInput" placeholder="e.g. EURUSD, US30, XAUUSD"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Primary timeframe context (optional note)</label><select id="timeframeInput"><option value="">Select…</option><option>Monthly</option><option>Weekly</option><option>Daily</option><option>4H</option><option>1H</option><option>30M</option><option>15M</option><option>5M</option><option>1M</option></select></div>
        </div>
        <div class="field"><label>Known context / upcoming events (optional — no live calendar feed, type what you know)</label><input type="text" id="contextInput" placeholder="e.g. FOMC in 3 hours, NFP tomorrow 8:30am"></div>
        <button class="primary" id="analyzeBtn" disabled style="margin-top:6px;width:100%;">Analyze Chart</button>
      </div>
      <div class="card" id="resultsCard" style="display:none;"><div class="card-title">2 &middot; AI Reading</div><div id="resultsBody"></div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="page" id="page-scanner">
      <div class="page-head"><h1 class="page-title">Batch Scanner &amp; Historical Upload</h1><p class="page-desc">Upload several charts at once — current setups to scan, or past charts to build historical reference data. Each gets the same AI read, ranked by confidence. On-demand batch analysis of what you upload, not a continuous live market scan. Markets do rhyme, but "Log as Pattern" builds a qualitative memory, not a proven statistical edge.</p></div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">Upload multiple charts</div>
        <div class="upload-zone" id="scannerUploadZone"><div style="font-size:20px;">&#8593;</div><p><strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Click to select multiple files</strong> (PNG/JPG, up to 8 at once)</p></div>
        <input type="file" id="scannerFileInput" accept="image/png,image/jpeg" multiple style="display:none;">
        <button class="primary" id="scannerRunBtn" disabled style="margin-top:12px;width:100%;">Scan Charts</button>
      </div>
      <div class="card" id="scannerResultsCard" style="display:none;"><div class="card-title">Ranked Results</div><div id="scannerResults"></div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="page" id="page-patterns">
      <div class="page-head"><h1 class="page-title">Pattern Library</h1><p class="page-desc">Log historical setups and how they played out — upload a result screenshot and the AI extracts the setup/outcome for you to review, or type it manually. Qualitative pattern reference the AI draws on during Analyze — not statistical backtesting (that needs full historical price series and simulation, which this tool doesn't have).</p></div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card-title">Log a Past Setup</div>
        <div class="field"><label>Optional: upload a screenshot of how the trade played out — fields below will auto-fill</label>
          <div class="upload-zone" id="patImageZone" style="min-height:90px;"><div style="font-size:16px;">&#8593;</div><p>Upload a result screenshot to auto-fill (optional)</p></div>
          <input type="file" id="patImageFile" accept="image/png,image/jpeg" style="display:none;">
          <div id="patExtractStatus" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="field-row3">
          <div class="field"><label>Symbol</label><input type="text" id="patSymbol" placeholder="EURUSD"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Timeframe</label><input type="text" id="patTf" placeholder="1H"></div>
          <div class="field"><label>Outcome</label><select id="patOutcome"><option value="win">Win</option><option value="loss">Loss</option><option value="be">Breakeven</option></select></div>
        </div>
        <div class="field"><label>Setup type / tag (e.g. "bullish OB retest", "liquidity sweep reversal")</label><input type="text" id="patSetupType"></div>
        <div class="field"><label>What happened — description of the setup and result</label><textarea id="patNotes" placeholder="Price swept the Asia low, reclaimed the OB on 15M, ran to the prior high for +2.4R…"></textarea></div>
        <div class="disclaimer" style="margin-bottom:12px;">The uploaded image is analyzed once to extract text, then discarded — not stored persistently (keeps storage light). Keep your own copy if you want the image itself.</div>
        <button class="primary" id="patSaveBtn">Save to Pattern Library</button>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px;">
        <div class="card-title">Library Insights<button class="small ghost" id="patInsightsBtn">Analyze My Pattern Library</button></div>
        <div id="patInsightsBox"><div class="empty-state">Run insights to see recurring conditions across your logged patterns.</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px;"><div class="card-title">Win Rate by Setup Type</div><div id="patStatsBox"></div></div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px;"><div class="card-title">Logged Patterns</div><div id="patternList"></div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="page" id="page-calculator">
      <div class="page-head"><h1 class="page-title">Risk &amp; Position Size Calculator</h1><p class="page-desc">Deterministic math — defaults are approximate; verify pip/point value against your Exness contract specification before sizing real trades.</p></div>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Inputs</div>
          <div class="field"><label>Symbol preset</label><select id="calcPreset"></select></div>
          <div class="field-row">
            <div class="field"><label>Account balance ($)</label><input type="number" id="calcBalance"></div>
            <div class="field"><label>Risk per trade (%)</label><input type="number" id="calcRiskPct" step="0.1"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="field-row">
            <div class="field"><label>Entry price</label><input type="number" id="calcEntry" step="any" placeholder="e.g. 1.0850"></div>
            <div class="field"><label>Stop loss price</label><input type="number" id="calcStop" step="any" placeholder="e.g. 1.0820"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="field-row">
            <div class="field"><label>Take profit price (optional)</label><input type="number" id="calcTP" step="any"></div>
            <div class="field"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="field-row">
            <div class="field"><label>Pip / point size</label><input type="number" id="calcPipSize" step="any"></div>
            <div class="field"><label>Value per pip/point, 1.0 lot ($)</label><input type="number" id="calcPipValue" step="any"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Result</div>
          <div class="grid" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px;">
            <div class="stat-box"><div class="stat-label">Risk amount</div><div class="stat-value gold" id="outRiskAmt">$0.00</div></div>
            <div class="stat-box"><div class="stat-label">Stop distance</div><div class="stat-value small" id="outStopDist">0</div></div>
            <div class="stat-box"><div class="stat-label">Position size</div><div class="stat-value small" id="outLots">0.00 lots</div></div>
            <div class="stat-box"><div class="stat-label">Reward:Risk</div><div class="stat-value small" id="outRR">—</div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="disclaimer" style="margin-top:14px;">Position size = risk amount ÷ (stop distance in pips/points × value per pip/point per 1.0 lot). Defaults are common approximations, not your broker's exact contract specs.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page" id="page-journal">
      <div class="page-head"><h1 class="page-title">Trading Journal</h1><p class="page-desc">Saved analyses and trades, stored on your server.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><div class="card-title">Entries<button class="small ghost" id="exportCsvBtn">Export CSV</button></div><div id="journalList"></div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="page" id="page-coach">
      <div class="page-head"><h1 class="page-title">AI Coach</h1><p class="page-desc">Evidence-based review of your closed trades — grounded in your actual journal, not generic advice.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><button class="primary" id="coachRunBtn">Review My Closed Trades</button><div id="coachStatus" style="margin-top:10px;"></div></div>
      <div class="card" id="coachResultsCard" style="display:none;"><div class="card-title">Coaching Review</div><div id="coachResults"></div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="page" id="page-stats">
      <div class="page-head"><h1 class="page-title">Performance Analytics</h1><p class="page-desc">Computed live from your journal entries.</p></div>
      <div class="grid grid-3" id="statsGrid"></div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px;"><div class="card-title">By Symbol</div><div id="statsBySymbol"></div></div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px;"><div class="card-title">By Session</div><div id="statsBySession"></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mobile-nav" id="navMobile"></div>

<button class="fl-toggle" id="flToggle" title="Franky Lamps">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" width="58" height="58" fill="none">
    <path d="M16 1 L3 9.5 L9 23 L15.5 18.5 L15.5 47 L32.5 47 L32.5 18.5 L39 23 L45 9.5 L32 1 C32 1 28.5 7 24 7 C19.5 7 16 1 16 1 Z" fill="#1F5FBF" stroke="#0F2E5E" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
    <text x="24" y="35" font-family="Anton, sans-serif" font-size="23" font-weight="400" fill="#fff" text-anchor="middle">8</text>
  </svg>
</button>
<div class="fl-panel" id="flPanel">
  <div class="fl-head">
    <div><div class="fl-head-title">Franky Lamps</div><div class="fl-head-sub">Same desk, same data — just conversational</div></div>
    <button class="fl-close" id="flClose">&times;</button>
  </div>
  <div class="fl-messages" id="flMessages">
    <div class="fl-msg assistant">Alright, alright — Franky here. Same brain as the rest of the desk, just better at small talk. I've got your settings, your journal, your last analysis, all of it. Ask me something quick — win rate on gold, what the last read said, whatever. I'll try not to make it weird.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="fl-input-row">
    <input type="text" id="flInput" placeholder="Ask Franky…">
    <button class="primary small" id="flSend">Send</button>
  </div>
</div>
<div id="authGate" style="display:none;position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(6,7,9,0.92);backdrop-filter:blur(6px);z-index:100;align-items:center;justify-content:center;">
  <div style="background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;padding:28px 26px;max-width:360px;width:90%;box-shadow:0 20px 60px -12px rgba(0,0,0,0.7);">
    <div style="font-family:'Anton',sans-serif;font-weight:400;font-size:19px;letter-spacing:0.02em;text-transform:uppercase;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--gold-bright),var(--gold));-webkit-background-clip:text;background-clip:text;color:transparent;margin-bottom:4px;">AI-B TRADING DESK</div>
    <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:12.5px;margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.5;">Enter the access token you configured as <code>APP_ACCESS_TOKEN</code> on your server. This keeps your Anthropic API key and your data private to you.</p>
    <div class="field"><input type="password" id="authGateInput" placeholder="Access token"></div>
    <button class="primary" id="authGateBtn" style="width:100%;">Unlock</button>
    <div id="authGateMsg" style="color:var(--bear);font-size:11.5px;margin-top:10px;min-height:14px;"></div>
  </div>
</div>
<script src="/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
